  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "When an owner wants to **convert an independent upper-upscale hotel**, the brands most commonly considered are the major **full-service upper-upscale** flags from Marriott, Hilton, IHG, Hyatt, Wyndham, and sometimes Accor/Choice. The most frequently cited options include **Marriott Hotels, Sheraton, Westin, Renaissance, Le Méridien, Autograph Collection, and Tribute Portfolio**; **Hilton, Curio Collection, Signia by Hilton, and Canopy by Hilton**; **InterContinental, Kimpton, Crowne Plaza, and Hotel Indigo**; **Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric, Grand Hyatt, and JdV by Hyatt**; and **Wyndham Grand, Dolce, and Registry Collection Hotels**.[1][2][4][7]\n\nFor a conversion specifically, the brands often highlighted as especially **conversion-friendly** are **Spark by Hilton** (though it is premium-economy rather than upper-upscale), **Garner by IHG**, and **City Express by Marriott**; these are discussed as examples of brands designed to make affiliation easier for existing independent properties.[2]\n\nIf you mean **upper-upscale conversion targets** rather than all hotel brands in the segment, the shortlist usually centers on:\n\n- **Marriott:** Marriott Hotels, Sheraton, Westin, Renaissance, Le Méridien, Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio[1][4]\n- **Hilton:** Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Signia by Hilton, Curio Collection, Canopy by Hilton[1][4]\n- **IHG:** InterContinental, Kimpton, Crowne Plaza, Hotel Indigo, Vignette Collection[1][4]\n- **Hyatt:** Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric, Grand Hyatt, JdV by Hyatt, Thompson Hotels[1]\n- **Wyndham:** Wyndham Grand, Registry Collection Hotels, Dolce Hotels & Resorts[7]\n- **Choice/Accor examples in the space:** Radisson Blu, Cambria, Pullman, Swissôtel, MGallery, Fairmont[1][5]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to the **best conversion brands by owner profile**: *soft brand vs hard brand*, *fee level*, or *minimum PIP tolerance*.",
